adjudication.rationale:
The new `sendAddGuestsEmails` implementation in `packages/emails/email-manager.ts` explicitly attempts to notify team members only when `calendarEvent.team?.members` is present:

```ts
if (calendarEvent.team?.members) {
  for (const teamMember of calendarEvent.team.members) {
    emailsToSend.push(sendEmail(() => new OrganizerAddGuestsEmail({ calEvent: calendarEvent, teamMember })));
  }
}
```

But the `CalendarEvent` object built in `addGuests.handler.ts` (`evt` around lines 120-146 in the diff) does not set any `team` field at all—only `organizer`, `attendees`, `type`, `location`, etc. Therefore `calendarEvent.team` will be `undefined` for this codepath, making the team-member notification loop unreachable and preventing co-hosts/team members from receiving the “guests added” organizer email.

This is a concrete, verifiable logic mismatch introduced in the diff (team notification code exists but cannot run with the constructed event payload).
